     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello everyone,<br><br>I am trying to implement WAIC for a simple case where the data comes from two multinomial distributions and am hoping to get feedback if my approach is correct. More precisely, WAIC requires the log-likelihood for each data point and sample, but with the inbuilt density function for the multinomial distribution we can only get the log likelihood for the whole multinomial distribution and not for the individual data points. Is it nevertheless appropriate to use WAIC in this case then?<br>For example, in my case I have two multinomials and then only get two log likelihoods per posterior sample.<br><br>A toy example follows below (using R and the loo package for WAIC).<br><br>Thanks,<br>Henrik<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rstan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>d </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> structure</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">db </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">200L</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1500L</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> bl </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4460</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3860</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> r </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6002</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5350</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> npl </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">988</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">905</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">11815</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">12930</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Names</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;db&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;r&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;npl&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;c&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> row</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">names </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2L</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">class</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;data.frame&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>d<br><br><br>m1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;<br>data { <br>  int&lt;lower=1&gt; n_200;<br>  int&lt;lower=1&gt; n_1500;<br>  int&lt;lower=0&gt; k_200[4];<br>  int&lt;lower=0&gt; k_1500[4];<br>}<br>parameters {<br>  real&lt;lower=0,upper=1&gt; c;<br>  real&lt;lower=0,upper=1&gt; r;<br>  real&lt;lower=0,upper=1&gt; u;<br>} <br>transformed parameters {<br>  simplex[4] theta;<br>  <br>  theta[1] &lt;- c;<br>  theta[2] &lt;- (1 - c) * r;<br>  theta[3] &lt;- (1 - c) * (1 - r) * u;<br>  theta[4] &lt;- (1 - c) * (1 - r) * (1 - u);<br>}<br>model {<br>  // Data<br>  k_200 ~ multinomial(theta);<br>  k_1500 ~ multinomial(theta);<br>}<br>generated quantities {<br>  real log_lik[2];<br>  <br>  log_lik[1] &lt;- multinomial_log(k_200, theta);<br>  log_lik[2] &lt;- multinomial_log(k_1500, theta);<br>}<br><br>&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>dat </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n_200 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">d</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> k_200 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> unlist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">d</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;c&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;r&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;npl&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)]),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>            n_1500 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">d</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> k_1500 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> unlist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">d</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;c&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;r&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;npl&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)])</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>samples </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model_code</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   <br>                 data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                 iter</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">loo</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>waic</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">extract_log_lik</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">samples</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## Computed from 2000 by 2 log-likelihood matrix</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">##           Estimate  SE</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## elpd_waic   -145.9 1.0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## p_waic        69.5 0.7</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## waic         291.8 2.1</span></div></code></div><br><br></div>"
